From 14ff1aca23a2b49f74fc8ebee1b92ea4c8adda32 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 19:41:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: push delivery, offline downloads, OpenAPI contract,
 Dart client

Backend
- Scheduled push (APNs + FCM) with timezone-correct firing and DST handling.
  Delivery is idempotent via UNIQUE(schedule_id, occurrence_key), so a restart
  or a second replica cannot wake a user twice.
- Push tokens are now persisted; previously accepted and silently discarded.
- FCM auth mints and refreshes its own OAuth2 tokens from a service-account
  key. The old pre-minted token expired within the hour and was never renewed.
- Offline downloads as time-bounded licences. Renewal re-checks entitlement,
  which is how a cancelled subscription eventually stops working offline.
- Refresh now rotates the session and detects reuse: replaying a retired token
  revokes the whole rotation chain.
- Persisted audit log, security metrics, split liveness/readiness probes.
- Fixed CI, which ran from the repo root and so compiled nothing.

Contract and client
- contracts/openapi.json generated from the live route table. Registration and
  documentation happen in one call, so the spec cannot drift from the server.
- clients/dart: typed client with domain models, offline cache and
  repositories. Concurrent 401s collapse onto a single refresh, otherwise
  parallel rotations would trip the server's reuse detection.

Fixes AudioAsset.URL leaking storage keys to clients.

404 Go tests, 35 Dart tests, race-clean.
